  "result": "{\"seen_before\": true, \"matches\": [\"PowerToys#44306\", \"PowerToys#38837\", \"PowerToys#25034\"], \"answer\": \"This has been reported before. Keyboard Manager only matches the exact shortcut you list, so a remap of Alt (Left)+Tab to Disabled does not apply once a third key such as W is held, and the system Alt+Tab still fires. The maintainers in PowerToys#44306 said this is by design. The only workaround they gave is to add a separate Disabled remap for each combination you want blocked, for example Alt+W+Tab. Keyboard Manager allows at most 2 modifiers plus 1 action key, so it cannot cover every combination. Older duplicates (PowerToys#38837, PowerToys#25034) were closed in favor of the tracking issue PowerToys#21850. Add your use case or a thumbs-up there if you want the behavior changed to ignore extra keys.\"}",
